es Staff/Faculty Job Openings Career Enrichment Breadcrumb Home Career Enrichment Career Enrichment at Lehigh (CE@L) features specialized tracks of courses, individualized learning plans, and other training opportunities suited to where you are now or where you want to go. Gain new insights and skills. Focus on trends in higher education, personal growth, and more. Take your career to new height or a totally new direction. Our Staff Lauren Hamory Learning Design and Development Specialist Email address: leh322@lehigh.edu Explore Upcoming Learning Opportunities See what professional development opportunities are available. PageUp Learning Management System Find courses and track your progress. LinkedIn Learning Enriching courses, certification paths and more. Nomination and High Potential Programs For Lehigh's accomplished and emerging leaders who have completed Essential Management or a comparable development course. Level up nomination/approval required. Learning Partners Find out more about the offices and organizations with whom we collaborate. Additional Resources Expand all View and Register for CE@L Programs Show the content Check out all of our programs currently available in our learning library. Follow this link. The BEST Program Show the content Learn more about the Build and Enhance Skills Through Training (BEST) program that supports the costs associated with enrolling in noncredit educational programs. Follow this link. Center for Innovation in Teaching and Learning Show the content The Center for Innovation in Teaching and Learning (CITL) in LTS fosters excellence in teaching, learning, and research. Follow this link. Tuition Benefits for Staff and Faculty Show the content Lehigh's tuition benefit program offers employees the opportunity to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees at the university and other LVAIC institutions. Follow this link. LTS Seminars Show the content LTS offers software and productivity workshops, including Qualtrics and G Suite, throughout the academic year. Follow this link. Vistex Institute For Executive Learning & Research Show the content Lehigh University's Vistex Institute For Executive Learning & Research offers open enrollment programs for individuals who want to add to their skills, build best practices, or develop their network. These programs are built for leaders and managers who want to be innovative, effective, knowledgeable and impactful in their work. Vistex offers a 50% tuition discount for Lehigh Faculty and Staff. Programs also may be supported by the BEST program. Sidebar Navigation Essentials (current) Show menu Disability Accommodations For Faculty and Staff Disability Accommodations Procedure Employee Relations When to Contact HR Reporting Bias and Harassment Employee Relations Resources Alternative Work Arrangements Flexplace and Remote Resources Lehigh Staff Flexplace Policy Completing a Flexplace Arrangement Request Staff, Researchers and Adjunct Faculty Fully Remote Policy Completing the Fully Remote Workplace Arrangement Request States Approved for Fully Remote Work Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware Florida Georgia Idaho Illinois Indiana Kansas Maryland Massachusetts Mississippi Missouri New Hampshire New Jersey New York North Carolina Ohio Oklahoma Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina Tennessee Texas Virginia Washington, D.C. West Virginia Wisconsin Employee Assistance Program Finance & Administration Inclusive Excellence and Belonging PageUp Learning, Performance and Talent User Guides Payroll Protection of Minors Compliance Report A Concern The Perch The Spot Well-Being Benefits & Rewards (current) Show menu Benefits Changes Effective January 1, 2027 Benefits Changes Taking Effect July 1, 2026 FY27 Changes to Vacation Accrual, Carryover and Payout Benefits Eligibility Staff Faculty Centennial School Employees Research Personnel Benefits-Eligible Retirees Temporary and/or Wage Employees Dependents Health Care Benefits Medical Insur