on Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 20 Nonexempt Staff Full-time 7 Locations Bethlehem 27 Fully Remote 2 Partial Remote 7 Categories Administrative Services 4 Athletics 1 Development/ Alumni Relations 4 Finance/Accounting 1 Health Care 1 Higher Education Administration 3 Human Resources 1 International Affairs 1 Library 1 Marketing/ Communication 1 Postdoc 5 Student Life 2 Technical/Scientific 1 Trades 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Web & Marketing Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Web & Marketing Coordinator provides key technical, administrative, and logistical support for the College of Education’s (COE) website, digital presence, and promotional activities. Reporting to the Marketing and Communications Manager, this role executes day-to-day web content updates, coordinates social media posting, and provides CMS support and guidance to faculty, staff, and departments under general supervision. Postdoctoral Research Associate in Control Systems, Artificial Intelligence, and Scientific Machine Learning for Fusion Energy Bethlehem The Lehigh University Plasma Control Group (LU-PCG) seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate in control systems engineering, AI, and scientific machine learning (SciML) for fusion energy. You will work on control synthesis, neural observers, scenario optimization, and AI digital twins for tokamak plasmas. Ideal for researchers in control theory, data science, ML, or plasma control looking to pioneer fusion solutions. Postdoctoral Research Associate in Computational Fusion Plasma Physics, Turbulence, Fast-Ion Transport, and AI-Enabled Modeling Bethlehem The Lehigh University Plasma Control Group (LU-PCG) seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate in computational fusion plasma physics. You will advance research on turbulent transport, energetic-particle physics, predictive modeling, and AI-enabled digital twins for magnetically confined tokamak plasmas. This role integrates high-fidelity simulations, reduced transport modeling, experimental validation, and machine learning to pioneer fusion energy solutions. Research and Finance Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Research and Finance Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the College of Health's research and business functions. The position is responsible for post-award research administration, payroll processing, purchasing and contract administration, and facilities and space management, ensuring compliance with university policies, sponsor requirements, and applicable regulations. Business Manager, Information and Technology Services Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Business Manager supports the effective operation of Information and Technology Services (ITS) by coordinating departmental business and administrative functions, including financial transactions, purchasing, vendor and contract administration, reporting, and related operational activities. The position assists the Director, Administration & Planning and serves as a resource to ITS leadership and staff on University business processes and works with internal and external partners to ensure administrative needs are addressed efficiently and in accordance with University policies and procedures. Coordinator - Pride Center Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Coordinator for The Pride Center at Lehigh University provides administrative and operational support to the Director and Associate Director, helping drive programs and initiatives that advance LGBTQ+ inclusion across campus. They will manage the Pride Center lounge, offering exceptional service and a welcoming space for students, faculty, and staff, while actively building strong partnerships with internal and external community constituents to foster a more inclusive campus environment. Assistant Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Assistant Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life is a 12-month professional position. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life. We seek a professional with passion for and a demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion, student advocacy, and student-centered learning and development. This position participates in departmental strategic planning and mission/vision development for Fraternity and Sorority Life. Program Manager Bethlehem The Program Manager serves as Lehigh University’s Alternate Representative to the United Nations. This unique role provides critical strategic and operational support, assisting in the facilitation of Lehigh’s engagement with United Nations Diplomats, Member States, NGO Presidents and Directors, and university-wide, specifically focusing on the development of youth leaders and the integration of UN-related opportunities into the university’s academic and experiential fabric. Postdoctoral Research Associate in the Center for Advancing Community Electrification Solutions (ACES) Bethlehem The ACES Center at Lehigh University seeks a Postdoctoral Researcher to investigate the stability and security of gigawatt-scale hyperscale data centers in inverter-dominated power grids. Working across ECE and CEE (Drs. Khazaei, Kishore, & Moazeni), you will explore complex dynamics between AI workloads, power electronics, UPS systems, and power grids. Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Administrative Coordinator for the Office of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs is a 12-month administrative position reporting to the Assistant Dean and Director of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs. We seek a professional with a passion for and strong expertise in administrative support, as this work is critical to the success of the fraternity and sorority community. Human Resources Assistant Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Human Resources Assistant provides foundational support primarily focused on benefits administration, data entry, and compliance support. This role supports employee benefits processes including enrollments, leave management, and payroll adjustments; ensures timely and accurate data entry; and assists with document management and compliance audits. As a key point of contact for general benefits inquiries, the assistant helps ensure a positive employee experience while supporting broader HR initiatives such as open enrollment, orientation, and benefit communications. Maintenance Technician Bethlehem Under General Supervision, performs skilled and experience tasks in building maintenance requiring the application of general knowledge of maintenance and repair procedures, materials, tools and equipment. At times, may need to work independently with minimal supervision and assistance. Language Specialist Bethlehem The International Center for Academic and Professional English (ICAPE) within OIA at Lehigh University comprises a dynamic group of instructors and administrators committed to excellence and best practices in the language and pragmatic instruction and support of Lehigh's graduate and undergraduate students, including their integration into the university community. ICAPE at Lehigh features advanced-level credit courses for matriculated students, as well as the pre-matriculation StepUp intensive English program, the TA program, and year-round individual tutoring and workshops in the English Language Lab. Instructional Staff responsibilities cross all areas of ICAPE's programs and include curriculum and instruction, assessment, administrative responsibilities, and professional development activities. Associate Director, Reunion and Affinity Giving Bethlehem The Associate Director is responsible for advancing annual philanthropic support through a combination of frontline fundraising and strategic development and coordination of the University’s Reunion and Affinity annual giving programs. Under the general supervision of the Senior Director of Annual Giving, this position will develop comprehensive and coordinated plans to increase annual philanthropic giving in honor of Reunion, as well as annual College-, Constituent- and/or Affinity-based giving. Financial Aid Coordinator, Student and Office Support Bethlehem The purpose of this non-exempt position is to provide administrative and clerical support to the Office of Financial Aid and Assistant Vice Provost of Financial Services and Director of Financial Aid by performing coordinator duties. Additionally, as a member of the Enrollment Support Coordinator team, this position is expected to provide superior customer service to students and families in the areas of both Admissions and Financial Aid. Assistant Coach, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field Bethlehem The Assistant Coach for Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field provides leadership, instruction, and operational support for Lehigh University's NCAA Division I Men's and Women's Cross Country and Track & Field programs. Reporting to the Head Cross Country and Track & Field Coaches, the Assistant Coach plays a vital role in advancing the mission of Lehigh University and the Department of Athletics through excellence in coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, championship event management, and program administration. Director, Corporate and Foundations Relations Bethlehem Reporting to the Assistant Vice President, College Development & University Initiatives, the Director, Corporate and Foundation Relations will work closely with assigned academic leaders to identify and pursue relationships and funding opportunities. The Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations will analyze and target a strategic portfolio of foundation partners, private foundations and other organizations, manage and grow a pipeline of prospects, and drive collaboration that results in increased philanthropy, sponsored research and internship/job opportunities. Program Director, Business Assistance Service Centers Bethlehem This position directs all operations and activities of the Lehigh SBDC’s Business Assistance Service Centers (BASC) in Lehigh and Northampton Counties.  The Program Director ensures that BASC services meet program objectives, deliver high-quality business assistance to area entrepreneurs, and comply with all contractual and reporting requirements established by the Pennsylvania Department of Community and Economic Development (DCED). Business Assistance Specialist Bethlehem Responsible for ensuring SBDC/BASC meets specific performance goals relative to individual service offerings as determined by Director. Provides consulting services to startup and existing businesses on strategies, business plans, cash flow projections, and other related matters as well as other Center programs. Investigates prepares and presents research to client on relevant topics. Responsible for preparing and coordinating program-specific training topics. Staff Physician Bethlehem The Staff Physician provides comprehensive primary care to university students in an ambulatory health setting. This role is responsible for the assessment, diagnosis, and management of acute and chronic health conditions, as well as preventive care and health promotion. The Staff Physician exercises advanced clinical judgment and evidence-based practice to support student health and ensure high-quality, compliant care delivery. More Jobs 7 Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Web & Marketing Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Web & Marketing Coordinator provides key technical, administrative, and logistical support for the College of Education’s (COE) website, digital presence, and promotional activities. Reporting to the Marketing and Communications Manager, this role executes day-to-day web content updates, coordinates social media posting, and provides CMS support and guidance to faculty, staff, and departments under general supervision. Postdoctoral Research Associate in Control Systems, Artificial Intelligence, and Scientific Machine Learning for Fusion Energy Bethlehem The Lehigh University Plasma Control Group (LU-PCG) seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate in control systems engineering, AI, and scientific machine learning (SciML) for fusion energy. You will work on control synthesis, neural observers, scenario optimization, and AI digital twins for tokamak plasmas. Ideal for researchers in control theory, data science, ML, or plasma control looking to pioneer fusion solutions. Postdoctoral Research Associate in Computational Fusion Plasma Physics, Turbulence, Fast-Ion Transport, and AI-Enabled Modeling Bethlehem The Lehigh University Plasma Control Group (LU-PCG) seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate in computational fusion plasma physics. You will advance research on turbulent transport, energetic-particle physics, predictive modeling, and AI-enabled digital twins for magnetically confined tokamak plasmas. This role integrates high-fidelity simulations, reduced transport modeling, experimental validation, and machine learning to pioneer fusion energy solutions. Research and Finance Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Research and Finance Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the College of Health's research and business functions. The position is responsible for post-award research administration, payroll processing, purchasing and contract administration, and facilities and space management, ensuring compliance with university policies, sponsor requirements, and applicable regulations. Business Manager, Information and Technology Services Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Business Manager supports the effective operation of Information and Technology Services (ITS) by coordinating departmental business and administrative functions, including financial transactions, purchasing, vendor and contract administration, reporting, and related operational activities. The position assists the Director, Administration & Planning and serves as a resource to ITS leadership and staff on University business processes and works with internal and external partners to ensure administrative needs are addressed efficiently and in accordance with University policies and procedures. Coordinator - Pride Center Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Coordinator for The Pride Center at Lehigh University provides administrative and operational support to the Director and Associate Director, helping drive programs and initiatives that advance LGBTQ+ inclusion across campus. They will manage the Pride Center lounge, offering exceptional service and a welcoming space for students, faculty, and staff, while actively building strong partnerships with internal and external community constituents to foster a more inclusive campus environment. Assistant Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Assistant Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life is a 12-month professional position. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life. We seek a professional with passion for and a demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion, student advocacy, and student-centered learning and development. This position participates in departmental strategic planning and mission/vision development for Fraternity and Sorority Life. Program Manager Bethlehem The Program Manager serves as Lehigh University’s Alternate Representative 