      "title": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Web & Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Web & Marketing Coordinator Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Human Resources Finance & Administration Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Essentials (current) Show menu Disability Accommodations For Faculty and Staff Disability Accommodations Procedure Employee Relations When to Contact HR Reporting Bias and Harassment Employee Relations Resources Alternative Work Arrangements Flexplace and Remote Resources Lehigh Staff Flexplace Policy Staff, Researchers and Adjunct Faculty Fully Remote Policy States Approved for Fully Remote Work Employee Assistance Program Finance & Administration Inclusive Excellence and Belonging PageUp Learning, Performance and Talent User Guides Payroll Protection of Minors Compliance Report A Concern The Perch The Spot Well-Being Benefits & Rewards (current) Show menu Benefits Changes Effective January 1, 2027 Benefits Changes Taking Effect July 1, 2026 FY27 Changes to Vacation Accrual, Carryover and Payout Benefits Eligibility Staff Faculty Centennial School Employees Research Personnel Benefits-Eligible Retirees Temporary and/or Wage Employees Dependents Health Care Benefits Medical Insurance Prescription Drug Coverage Behavioral (Mental) Health Benefits Vision Care Dental Coverage Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Adult Vaccine Benefits for Lehigh Medical Plan Participants Medicare Eligibility & Your Coverage Options Worker’s Compensation Compensation Market Referenced Job Evaluation Process Lehigh Staff Salary Structure Lehigh University Compensation Philosophy Variable Pay Time Away From Work Short Term Disability Staff Paid Parental Leave Benefit Retirement And Financial Security Lehigh Retirement Plan Social Security and Medicare Basic And Supplemental Life Insurance Dependent Life Insurance Long Term Disability Insurance Educational Benefits Education Benefits For Faculty and Staff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Nonexempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Partial Remote 1 Categories Marketing/ Communication 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Web & Marketing Coordinator Apply now Job no: 504024 Work type: Nonexempt Staff Full-time Location: Partial Remote, Bethlehem Categories: Marketing/ Communication Lehigh University's College of Education is shaping the next generation of educators, counselors, and school leaders. If you're someone who takes pride in keeping digital content sharp, organized, and working hard for its audience, this is a role where your attention to detail makes a real difference. Reporting to the Marketing and Communications Manager, you'll keep the College of Education's digital presence accurate, current, and engaging. Position Number: S71150 This position is a Grade: 8 - 37.5 with an approximate salary range of $44,600- $53,530 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. What You'll Be Doing Executing web content updates and maintaining the COE website using the university's content management system (CMS) Coordinating and scheduling social media content across the college's platforms, including drafting copy and sourcing imagery Providing CMS guidance and hands-on support to faculty, staff, and departments across the college Monitoring website analytics and preparing regular reports to inform content decisions Assisting in the production of digital and print marketing materials, including newsletters, flyers, and event collateral Supporting the planning and promotion of college events, open days, and recruitment campaigns Coordinating photo and video asset management, ensuring materials are organized and accessible for ongoing use Liaising with Lehigh's central marketing and communications teams to ensure brand consistency across all COE channels Responding to internal requests for web and communications support, triaging and prioritizing tasks effectively What You Bring Associates or Vocational/Technical Degree in Marketing, Communications, Web Design, Information Technology, or a related field One to three years of related work experience Demonstrated experience working with a CMS platform (such as WordPress, Drupal, or similar) Solid understanding of social media platforms and content scheduling tools Strong written communication skills with a careful eye for accuracy and consistency Ability to manage multiple requests and deadlines while working under general supervision Experience in a higher education or similarly complex organizational environment is highly regarded Comfort working collaboratively with faculty and professional staff who have varying levels of digital fluency Why Lehigh and the College of Education Lehigh University offers a genuinely supportive work environment within a research-active institution that values both academic excellence and professional development. As a staff member, you'll have access to generous benefits including above-standard retirement contributions, substantial tuition benefits for employees and eligible family members, and competitive leave entitlements. The work you do in the College of Education directly supports faculty and students driving meaningful change in schools and communities across the region. This is not a generic coordinator role; it sits inside a college with a distinct identity, and you'll be a valued part of communicating that story. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: September 03, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Web & Marketing Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Web & Marketing Coordinator provides key technical, administrative, and logistical support for the College of Education’s (COE) website, digital presence, and promotional activities. Reporting to the Marketing and Communications Manager, this role executes day-to-day web content updates, coordinates social media posting, and provides CMS support and guidance to faculty, staff, and departments under general supervision. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Web & Marketing Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Web & Marketing Coordinator provides key technical, administrative, and logistical support for the College of Education’s (COE) website, digital presence, and promotional activities. Reporting to the Marketing and Communications Manager, this role executes day-to-day web content updates, coordinates social media posting, and provides CMS support and guidance to faculty, staff, and departments under general supervision. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
