fits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Nonexempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Partial Remote 1 Categories Administrative Services 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Research and Finance Coordinator Apply now Job no: 504019 Work type: Nonexempt Staff Full-time Location: Partial Remote, Bethlehem Categories: Administrative Services As Research and Finance Coordinator, you will sit at the intersection of sponsored research, financial operations, and facilities management, providing the administrative infrastructure that allows faculty to focus on their work. This is a role for someone who takes genuine satisfaction in building systems, solving problems, and being the person others rely on to get things right. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and university partners, you will serve as a key resource for operational guidance, financial stewardship, and administrative coordination. In addition to managing day-to-day operations, you will be expected to identify opportunities to improve processes, enhance operational efficiency, and develop effective administrative practices that support the College's continued growth and strategic priorities. Position Number: S71350 This position is a Grade: 8 - 37.5 with an approximate salary range of $44,600-$53,530 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. The Work You Will Do Review terms and conditions of newly awarded or amended grants, establish faculty financial indices, monitor budgets, reconcile expenditures, and prepare financial reports and projections for faculty and college leadership Identify budget variances, recommend corrective actions, and process reallocations to ensure effective stewardship of sponsored and college funds in accordance with OMB Uniform Guidance and institutional policy Assist faculty investigators with grant related inquiries, expense planning, compliance issues, and agreement review, and facilitate timely submission of progress reports and financial statements to internal offices Manage payroll processing for undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, post doctoral, and other research personnel, including appointment paperwork, offer letters, and quarterly Effort Certification reviews Coordinate purchasing and procurement activities, managing purchase requisitions, purchase orders, accounts payable and receivable, and routing contracts and service agreements in partnership with Procurement, General Counsel, and Research and Sponsored Programs Serve as the primary liaison with Facilities Services on space planning, office and laboratory assignments, renovation projects, maintenance requests, and capital improvements aligned with the College's strategic growth What You Bring Associates or Vocational/Technical Degree or related field Three to five years of work related experience Candidates who do not possess an Associate’s Degree but have a high school diploma and at least 5 years of highly related experience may also be considered based on the relevance and depth of their experience Experience in research administration, grant coordination, or a comparable finance and operations role, ideally within a higher education or research intensive environment Demonstrated ability to manage payroll workflows across multiple funding sources with accuracy and discretion Strong organizational skills and a track record of managing competing deadlines across a broad portfolio of responsibilities Clear, confident communication skills for working across university offices including Procurement, General Counsel, Facilities, and Research and Sponsored Programs Why Lehigh and the College of Health Lehigh University offers a collegial, research rich environment where staff are recognized as integral to the institution's mission. The College of Health is one of Lehigh's newest and most actively expanding academic communities, meaning the work you do here will have a direct and visible impact on how the College grows and operates. Lehigh provides generous retirement contributions, robust tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents, and a campus culture built around collaboration and long term professional development. This is a full time, nonexempt staff position where your expertise will be put to use from the very beginning. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to 