nd Staff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Partial Remote 1 Categories Finance/Accounting 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Business Manager, Information and Technology Services Apply now Job no: 504016 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Partial Remote, Bethlehem Categories: Finance/Accounting Lehigh University's Information and Technology Services (ITS) division keeps a research-intensive university running and the Business Manager role sits at the center of making that happen. If you thrive on bringing order to complexity and want your operational expertise to directly support academic and research excellence, this is a role worth your attention. Position Number: S77690 This position is a Grade: 9 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $56,030-$68,190 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. What You'll Own Coordinate the full range of departmental business and administrative functions across ITS, ensuring day-to-day operations align with University policies and procedures Manage financial transactions, purchasing activity, and vendor relationships, supporting accurate and timely processing across the division Administer contracts and service agreements, serving as a key point of contact for internal and external partners on procurement and compliance matters Prepare operational and financial reports that equip ITS leadership and the Director, Administration & Planning with the information needed to make sound decisions Monitor budget activity, track expenditures, and flag variances to support sound fiscal management across ITS cost centers Serve as a resource to ITS staff on University business processes, helping teams navigate administrative requirements efficiently and with confidence Coordinate onboarding and offboarding administrative tasks for ITS staff, including equipment procurement, system access requests, and space management Support planning and coordination of divisional initiatives, including scheduling, documentation, and follow-through on action items for ITS leadership Liaise with central University departments — including Finance, Procurement, and Human Resources — to ensure ITS administrative needs are addressed in a timely manner Identify opportunities to streamline administrative workflows and contribute to continuous improvement across ITS business operations What You Bring Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, Business Administration, or related field Three to five years of work related experience Demonstrated experience in business administration, financial coordination, or operational management — ideally within higher education or a comparably structured organization Solid working knowledge of purchasing, accounts payable, and contract administration processes Proven ability to interpret and apply institutional policies, translating them into clear guidance for staff and stakeholders Strong analytical skills with experience producing clear, accurate financial or operational reports A collaborative approach to working across organizational boundaries, including with technology teams, finance, and external vendors Why Lehigh Lehigh University is a private research university with a distinct culture of collaboration between faculty, staff, and students in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania. As a staff member, you'll have access to generous tuition benefits , comprehensive health coverage, strong retirement contributions, and a campus community that genuinely values the people who keep it moving. ITS is a division where your contributions are visible and where leadership actively invests in the professional growth of its team. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. This position has fiscal or financial responsibilities other than employee expense activity, such as processing or approving transactions; monitoring or preparing budgets; or generating income for University, therefore a credit check is required. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 26, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Business Manager, Information and Technology Services Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Business Manager supports the effective operation of Information and Technology Services (ITS) by coordinating departmental business and administrative functions, including financial transactions, purchasing, vendor and contract administration, reporting, and related operational activities. The position assists the Director, Administration & Planning and serves as a resource to ITS leadership and staff on University business processes and works with internal and external partners to ensure administrative needs are addressed efficiently and in accordance with University policies and procedures. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Business Manager, Information and Technology Services Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Business Manager supports the effective operation of Information and Technology Services (ITS) by coordinating departmental business and administrative functions, including financial transactions, purchasing, vendor and contract administration, reporting, and related operational activities. The position assists the Director, Administration & Planning and serves as a resource to ITS leadership and staff on University business processes and works with internal and external partners to ensure administrative needs are addressed efficiently and in accordance with University policies and procedures. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
