newsletter, maintaining the website, managing social media, and creating flyers, graphics, and promotional materials for events and tabling Build and maintain partnerships across campus and the wider community by serving on institutional committees, liaising with community partners, supporting alumni and donor communications, and contributing to broader Inclusive Excellence and Belonging (OIEB) initiatives and events What You Bring High School Diploma or GED One to three years of work related experience Experience in administrative coordination within higher education, student services, or a community-focused setting Confidence managing budgets, tracking expenditures, and working within financial systems such as Banner Strong digital communications skills including social media management, content creation, and website maintenance Highly organized with the ability to juggle multiple priorities, identify process improvements, and follow through independently A genuine service orientation — you take pride in creating spaces where every person feels seen, supported, and welcomed Why Lehigh Lehigh University offers a rich environment where staff are recognized as essential contributors to the academic mission. You'll join the Inclusive Excellence & Belonging department at a moment of genuine institutional investment in equity and belonging. Lehigh's comprehensive benefits include generous leave, strong retirement contributions, tuition benefits for employees and eligible family members, and access to a vibrant campus community in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania. Here, your work has a direct line to student wellbeing — that impact is visible and real every day. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or 