s Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Partial Remote 1 Categories Student Life 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Assistant Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life Apply now Job no: 504015 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Partial Remote, Bethlehem Categories: Student Life Fraternity and sorority communities thrive when they're supported by professionals who genuinely invest in student growth. At Lehigh University, Fraternity and Sorority Life is looking for an Assistant Director who brings both strategic thinking and a deep commitment to inclusive, student-centered practice. Reporting to the Associate Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life, you'll play an active role in shaping the direction of a department that takes its educational mission seriously. Position Number: S83340 This position is a Grade: 8 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $47,570-$57,090 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. What You'll Be Doing Advising assigned fraternity and sorority chapters and governing councils in their development, accountability, and community engagement Contributing to departmental strategic planning and the ongoing refinement of the office's mission and vision Designing and facilitating student-centered programs that advance diversity, equity, and inclusion within Greek-letter communities Overseeing recruitment, intake, and new member education processes to ensure alignment with university policy and chapter values Managing conduct and accountability processes for assigned chapters, partnering with the Dean of Students office where appropriate Delivering risk management education and supporting chapters in building cultures of care and informed decision-making Collecting and analyzing community data to inform assessment, reporting, and continuous program improvement Serving as a consistent advocate for students, connecting them with resources across the broader Student Affairs division What You Bring Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, or equivalent combination of education and experience One to three years of work related experience A track record of developing inclusive programs that reflect a commitment to equity and belonging Experience in student conduct, conflict resolution, and community standards work Experience contributing to strategic planning or departmental goal-setting processes Solid computer skills needed to handle campus management software Exercises sound judgment and problem-solving skills Excellent presentation skills Good communication and interpersonal skills Why Lehigh Lehigh University is a research-intensive institution in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, where Student Affairs professionals are genuine partners in the academic mission. This 12-month, full-time position comes with strong retirement contributions, tuition benefits , and professional development support — within a department that values substance and measurable student impact. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. This position is funded by soft dollars; there is no severance associated with this position. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 26, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Assistant Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Assistant Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life is a 12-month professional position. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life. We seek a professional with passion for and a demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion, student advocacy, and student-centered learning and development. This position participates in departmental strategic planning and mission/vision development for Fraternity and Sorority Life. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Assistant Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Assistant Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life is a 12-month professional position. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life. We seek a professional with passion for and a demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion, student advocacy, and student-centered learning and development. This position participates in departmental strategic planning and mission/vision development for Fraternity and Sorority Life. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
