esources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Nonexempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Partial Remote 1 Categories Administrative Services 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Coordinator Apply now Job no: 504002 Work type: Nonexempt Staff Full-time Location: Partial Remote, Bethlehem Categories: Administrative Services Lehigh University's Division of Student Affairs is home to programs that shape the undergraduate experience in meaningful ways — and the Office of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs is no exception. If you're a detail-oriented administrative professional who finds genuine satisfaction in keeping a busy, people-centered office running smoothly, this full-time Coordinator role offers the chance to do exactly that within one of Lehigh's most active student communities. Reporting to the Assistant Dean and Director of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs, you'll be the operational backbone of an office that supports dozens of chapters and hundreds of students. Position Number: S77590 This position is a Grade: 7 - 37.5 with an approximate salary range of $37,190-$44,640 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. What You'll Be Doing Managing office workflows, scheduling, correspondence, and records to keep the team focused and organized Coordinating logistics for programs, events, and chapter-related activities across the academic year Maintaining accurate databases, tracking compliance documentation, and preparing reports for leadership Serving as a first point of contact for students, chapter advisors, and campus partners, providing responsive and knowledgeable support Tracking chapter and student account balances and flagging discrepancies in a timely manner Executing registration processes for chapters, members, and associated programs throughout the year Updating and maintaining the office website to ensure content is current and accessible to students and stakeholders Supporting educational initiatives and community programming that advance the goals of the fraternity and sorority community What You Bring Associate's degree or higher, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience Three to five years of work related experience Proven experience in administrative coordination or office management, ideally within higher education or a comparable environment Strong organizational skills with an ability to manage competing priorities without dropping the detail Clear written and verbal communication skills suited to a student-facing setting Demonstrated customer service skills, including the ability to respond professionally and promptly to phone calls, emails, and walk-in enquiries from a range of constituents including students, parents, alumni, and community members Proficiency with standard office and database software; comfort learning university-specific systems at Lehigh A collaborative, service-oriented approach that reflects Lehigh's commitment to student success and community integrity Why Lehigh Lehigh University offers a genuinely supportive working environment on a residential campus in Bethlehem, PA, where staff are valued contributors to student life — not just behind-the-scenes operators. This 12-month position comes with access to Lehigh's generous benefits package, including tuition benefits, retirement contributions above standard rates, and substantial paid leave. You'll work alongside a director who is invested in your professional development and within a division that takes student wellbeing seriously at every level. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 13, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Administrative Coordinator for the Office of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs is a 12-month administrative position reporting to the Assistant Dean and Director of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs. We seek a professional with a passion for and strong expertise in administrative support, as this work is critical to the success of the fraternity and sorority community. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Coordinator Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Administrative Coordinator for the Office of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs is a 12-month administrative position reporting to the Assistant Dean and Director of Fraternity and Sorority Affairs. We seek a professional with a passion for and strong expertise in administrative support, as this work is critical to the success of the fraternity and sorority community. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
