r Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Nonexempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Partial Remote 1 Categories Human Resources 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Human Resources Assistant Apply now Job no: 504006 Work type: Nonexempt Staff Full-time Location: Partial Remote, Bethlehem Categories: Human Resources Lehigh University's Human Resources team is looking for a detail-oriented Human Resources Assistant to help ensure that Lehigh's faculty and staff receive accurate, timely benefits support from day one. If you're someone who finds satisfaction in getting the details right and genuinely enjoys helping people navigate their workplace benefits, this role offers a meaningful entry point into higher education HR. Position Number: S78040 This position is a Grade: 7 - 37.5 with an approximate salary range of $37,190-$44,640 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. What You'll Be Doing Processing benefits enrollments, changes, and leave management requests with accuracy and within established timelines Maintaining employee data in HR systems and supporting payroll adjustments related to benefits activity Assisting with compliance audits and document management to meet federal, state, and university policy requirements Serving as a first point of contact for general benefits enquiries, guiding employees through their options with clarity and care Contributing to key HR events including open enrollment Coordinating leave of absence administration, including tracking employee leave balances and ensuring documentation is complete and current Supporting the preparation and distribution of benefits-related communications to faculty and staff across the university Reconciling benefits invoices and flagging discrepancies for review in collaboration with payroll and finance teams Assisting with the maintenance of HR records in accordance with Lehigh's records retention policies and applicable regulations Providing general administrative support to the HR department, including scheduling, correspondence, and responding to routine HR enquiries What You'll Bring High School Diploma or GED One to three years of work related experience Experience in an administrative, HR, or benefits support role — or demonstrated equivalent capability Strong data entry skills with a track record of accuracy and attention to detail Comfortable handling sensitive employee information with discretion and confidentiality Clear written and verbal communication skills, particularly when explaining complex benefits information to employees Familiarity with HRIS platforms and standard office productivity tools Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a structured, compliance-conscious environment like Lehigh's centralized HR model Why Lehigh Lehigh University brings together a close-knit academic community in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, with a genuine commitment to the wellbeing of its people. As a staff member, you'll have access to generous tuition benefits , above-standard retirement contributions, comprehensive health coverage, and significant leave entitlements, reflecting the University's long-standing investment in its workforce. The HR team operates with a collaborative, service-first culture where your contributions to process accuracy and employee experience have a direct impact on the broader university community. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 13, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Human Resources Assistant Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Human Resources Assistant provides foundational support primarily focused on benefits administration, data entry, and compliance support. This role supports employee benefits processes including enrollments, leave management, and payroll adjustments; ensures timely and accurate data entry; and assists with document management and compliance audits. As a key point of contact for general benefits inquiries, the assistant helps ensure a positive employee experience while supporting broader HR initiatives such as open enrollment, orientation, and benefit communications. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Human Resources Assistant Partial Remote, Bethlehem The Human Resources Assistant provides foundational support primarily focused on benefits administration, data entry, and compliance support. This role supports employee benefits processes including enrollments, leave management, and payroll adjustments; ensures timely and accurate data entry; and assists with document management and compliance audits. As a key point of contact for general benefits inquiries, the assistant helps ensure a positive employee experience while supporting broader HR initiatives such as open enrollment, orientation, and benefit communications. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
