    "http://careers.pageuppeople.com/865/cw/en-us/job/504003/maintenance-technician": {
      "title": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Maintenance Technician Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Human Resources Finance & Administration Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Essentials (current) Show menu Disability Accommodations For Faculty and Staff Disability Accommodations Procedure Employee Relations When to Contact HR Reporting Bias and Harassment Employee Relations Resources Alternative Work Arrangements Flexplace and Remote Resources Lehigh Staff Flexplace Policy Staff, Researchers and Adjunct Faculty Fully Remote Policy States Approved for Fully Remote Work Employee Assistance Program Finance & Administration Inclusive Excellence and Belonging PageUp Learning, Performance and Talent User Guides Payroll Protection of Minors Compliance Report A Concern The Perch The Spot Well-Being Benefits & Rewards (current) Show menu Benefits Changes Effective January 1, 2027 Benefits Changes Taking Effect July 1, 2026 FY27 Changes to Vacation Accrual, Carryover and Payout Benefits Eligibility Staff Faculty Centennial School Employees Research Personnel Benefits-Eligible Retirees Temporary and/or Wage Employees Dependents Health Care Benefits Medical Insurance Prescription Drug Coverage Behavioral (Mental) Health Benefits Vision Care Dental Coverage Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Adult Vaccine Benefits for Lehigh Medical Plan Participants Medicare Eligibility & Your Coverage Options Worker’s Compensation Compensation Market Referenced Job Evaluation Process Lehigh Staff Salary Structure Lehigh University Compensation Philosophy Variable Pay Time Away From Work Short Term Disability Staff Paid Parental Leave Benefit Retirement And Financial Security Lehigh Retirement Plan Social Security and Medicare Basic And Supplemental Life Insurance Dependent Life Insurance Long Term Disability Insurance Educational Benefits Education Benefits For Faculty and Staff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Nonexempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Trades 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Maintenance Technician Apply now Job no: 504003 Work type: Nonexempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Trades Lehigh University's campus is a landmark of history and innovation — and keeping it that way takes genuine skill. If you take pride in hands-on work that makes a real difference to the people who live, learn, and work around you, this is a role worth exploring. As a Maintenance Technician within the Facilities department, you'll carry out skilled building maintenance and repair work across Lehigh's distinctive campus. Working under general supervision, you'll apply broad maintenance knowledge to deliver reliable, high-quality outcomes — and at times, you'll manage tasks independently, drawing on your own expertise to get the job done. Position Number: S75900 This position is a Grade: 8 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $47,570-$57,090 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. What You'll Be Doing Perform skilled maintenance and repair tasks across campus buildings, including mechanical, structural, and general facilities work Apply working knowledge of materials, tools, and equipment appropriate to each task Identify maintenance issues promptly and carry out effective repairs with minimal rework Interpret and action work orders accurately, ensuring tasks are completed to standard Conduct routine inspections and preventative maintenance to reduce unplanned failures Respond to maintenance requests in a timely manner, minimizing disruption to campus operations Maintain accurate records of work completed, materials used, and any follow-up requirements Operate independently when required, prioritizing safety and quality throughout Collaborate with Facilities colleagues to coordinate scheduling and share technical knowledge What You'll Bring High School Diploma or Ged; Associates or Vocational/Technical degree preferred or equivalent combination of education and experience Three to five years of work related experience Valid driver's license with a good driving record Demonstrated experience in building maintenance or a closely related trade Solid working knowledge of general maintenance and repair procedures across multiple disciplines Ability to read work orders and apply the right materials and tools for each job Comfort working both within a team and independently with minimal oversight A methodical approach to problem-solving on the job Familiarity with safety protocols in a facilities or institutional environment Why Lehigh Lehigh University is a research-intensive institution with a strong commitment to its people — including those who keep the campus running. As a full-time staff member, you'll have access to generous leave benefits , above-standard retirement contributions, and meaningful study assistance programs. The Facilities team is known for its collaborative culture and shared sense of purpose: this isn't anonymous maintenance work — you'll see the direct impact of what you do every day across a campus community that values every team member's contribution. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of the position do not allow for a remote work option; the employee in this position will be required to work on campus where they can be fully accessible to the Lehigh community. This position is responsible for driving University-owned vehicles as a routine function, therefore a valid Driver’s License and a good driving record is required. This position has direct contact with minors, therefore, a background check is required. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 12, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Maintenance Technician Bethlehem Under General Supervision, performs skilled and experience tasks in building maintenance requiring the application of general knowledge of maintenance and repair procedures, materials, tools and equipment. At times, may need to work independently with minimal supervision and assistance. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Maintenance Technician Bethlehem Under General Supervision, performs skilled and experience tasks in building maintenance requiring the application of general knowledge of maintenance and repair procedures, materials, tools and equipment. At times, may need to work independently with minimal supervision and assistance. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
