ses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Higher Education Administration 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Language Specialist Apply now Job no: 503997 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Higher Education Administration S99490 Language Specialist Position Purpose: The International Center for Academic and Professional English (ICAPE) within OIA at Lehigh University comprises a dynamic group of instructors and administrators committed to excellence and best practices in the language and pragmatic instruction and support of Lehigh's graduate and undergraduate students, including their integration into the university community. ICAPE at Lehigh features advanced-level credit courses for matriculated students, as well as the pre-matriculation StepUp intensive English program, the TA program, and year-round individual tutoring and workshops in the English Language Lab. Instructional Staff responsibilities cross all areas of ICAPE's programs and include curriculum and instruction, assessment, administrative responsibilities, and professional development activities. This position is a Grade: 9 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $56,030-$68,190 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities 1. Curriculum and Instruction *teach a minimum of three courses per 16-week semester (or the equivalent in instructional units), which may include a combination of credit and non-credit courses, ongoing seminars and workshops, as well as scheduled work with students at the English Language Lab. *Submit all student grades, evaluations, and other student assessments by the stated deadlines. *Attend and participate in ICAPE program curriculum development, instructor and staff meetings, textbook selection, portfolio evaluations, course assessments, orientations, graduations, committee work, performance reviews, and other ICAPE program initiatives and activities. *Assist with the creation, design, and implementation of new or revised ICAPE courses and programs that meet evolving student and institutional needs and goals. 2. Assessment *Assist with assessing the English language proficiency of students. *Administer, rate, report, develop, pilot, and maintain all English proficiency assessments. *Participate in teaching assistant English fluency exam administrations as an ICAPE evaluator. *Assist with the creation, piloting, and implementation of new English fluency assessments. *Assist with revisions of current English language assessments, including but not limited to the Test of Pedagogical Speaking Skills (TOPSS) design, descriptors, and testing protocol. 3. Administrative *Hold a minimum of two drop-in office hours per week , when classes are in session. *Advise students and participate in student file preparation and maintenance. *Assist with ICAPE program tasks and activities. 4. Professional Development *stay updated on current TESOL research, best practices, technology, and other trends in TESOL. *Serve on ICAPE and/or university committees and participate in initiatives, events, training, and other activities. Qualifications Master’s Degree in TESOL, Linguistics, Education, or a directly related field. At least three years of work experience as a Language Specialist or in a closely related position. Why Lehigh Lehigh sits at the intersection of rigorous research, close-knit community, and a proud legacy of innovation rooted in Bethlehem, PA. You will join a collaborative Office of General Counsel where your expertise will genuinely shape institutional decision-making. Lehigh offers a strong benefits package including generous leave provisions, above-market retirement contributions, and robust professional development support, including access to the University's own academic resources. This is an institution that takes compliance seriously, and gives its compliance leadership the standing to match. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist. Special Considerations The duties of this position may allow the employee to work partially remote as deemed appropriate by their supervisor. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 10, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Language Specialist Bethlehem The International Center for Academic and Professional English (ICAPE) within OIA at Lehigh University comprises a dynamic group of instructors and administrators committed to excellence and best practices in the language and pragmatic instruction and support of Lehigh's graduate and undergraduate students, including their integration into the university community. ICAPE at Lehigh features advanced-level credit courses for matriculated students, as well as the pre-matriculation StepUp intensive English program, the TA program, and year-round individual tutoring and workshops in the English Language Lab. Instructional Staff responsibilities cross all areas of ICAPE's programs and include curriculum and instruction, assessment, administrative responsibilities, and professional development activities. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Language Specialist Bethlehem The International Center for Academic and Professional English (ICAPE) within OIA at Lehigh University comprises a dynamic group of instructors and administrators committed to excellence and best practices in the language and pragmatic instruction and support of Lehigh's graduate and undergraduate students, including their integration into the university community. ICAPE at Lehigh features advanced-level credit courses for matriculated students, as well as the pre-matriculation StepUp intensive English program, the TA program, and year-round individual tutoring and workshops in the English Language Lab. Instructional Staff responsibilities cross all areas of ICAPE's programs and include curriculum and instruction, assessment, administrative responsibilities, and professional development activities. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability