ff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Development/ Alumni Relations 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Associate Director, Reunion and Affinity Giving Apply now Job no: 503995 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Development/ Alumni Relations Lehigh University's Development and Alumni Relations team is looking for a strategic and relationship-driven fundraiser to lead Reunion and Affinity Giving programs that connect thousands of alumni to the University's mission. If you bring a sharp eye for data, a genuine enthusiasm for donor engagement, and the ability to turn collaborative plans into measurable results, this role offers real scope to shape giving culture at a nationally recognized research university. Position Number: S80620 This position is a Grade: 10 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $67,270-$81,830 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities Cultivate, solicit, and steward a dynamic portfolio of Reunion and Affinity prospects through in-person/digital visits, strategic outreach, and tailored communications to assess donor capacity and passion. Drive unrestricted gifts for the Lehigh Fund by executing multi-channel strategies, preparing high-quality donor briefings and proposals, and ensuring prospects are solicited for the appropriate giving levels. Partner with DAR College Partners, Senior Directors, and Associate Deans to design direct response plans (direct mail, email, digital) aligned with institutional fundraising priorities and unified messaging across all five colleges. Manage end-to-end campaign timelines, vendors, and copywriting deliverables while collaborating with Information Systems to ensure precise audience segmentation, data integrity, and on-schedule campaign launches. Design and execute a comprehensive annual giving plan for Reunion classes by collaborating with Individual Giving, Alumni Relations, Planned Giving, and Family Philanthropy to align mass solicitations, events, and individual prospect strategies. Drive milestone reunion giving by leveraging events and cross-departmental partnerships to maximize high-impact, unrestricted support for the Lehigh Fund. Serve as the primary liaison for University constituent and affinity groups, partnering with Alumni Relations and Information Systems to define audience targets, evaluate direct-response channels, and elevate annual giving support. Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and external vendors to design, coordinate, and launch integrated, multi-channel fundraising initiatives across direct mail, digital, and crowdfunding platforms. Partner with Donor Relations to build and evaluate targeted donor stewardship plans while continually analyzing campaign performance to optimize future solicitation strategies. Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Business, Communications, Marketing or a related field Three to five years of work related experience Fundraising experience or experience in higher education would be preferred Strong communications and marketing experience preferred Strong project management skills with the ability to coordinate across departments and competing priorities A data-informed approach to strategy with comfort using CRM or fundraising platforms Why Lehigh Lehigh University has a long-standing reputation for academic excellence and a fiercely loyal alumni community — assets that make fundraising here genuinely rewarding. As part of DAR, you'll work alongside colleagues who care deeply about the mission and bring real expertise to the table. Lehigh offers an exceptional benefits package including generous paid leave, above-benchmark retirement contributions, tuition benefits for employees and dependents, and a campus environment that balances intellectual rigor with genuine warmth. This is a place where your strategic ideas will find space to grow. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations This position will include some weekends and evening work as necessary for special university events. The duties of the position do not allow for a remote work option; the employee in this position will be required to work on campus where they can be fully accessible to the Lehigh community. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: August 07, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Associate Director, Reunion and Affinity Giving Bethlehem The Associate Director is responsible for advancing annual philanthropic support through a combination of frontline fundraising and strategic development and coordination of the University’s Reunion and Affinity annual giving programs. Under the general supervision of the Senior Director of Annual Giving, this position will develop comprehensive and coordinated plans to increase annual philanthropic giving in honor of Reunion, as well as annual College-, Constituent- and/or Affinity-based giving. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Associate Director, Reunion and Affinity Giving Bethlehem The Associate Director is responsible for advancing annual philanthropic support through a combination of frontline fundraising and strategic development and coordination of the University’s Reunion and Affinity annual giving programs. Under the general supervision of the Senior Director of Annual Giving, this position will develop comprehensive and coordinated plans to increase annual philanthropic giving in honor of Reunion, as well as annual College-, Constituent- and/or Affinity-based giving. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
