nd Staff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Nonexempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Administrative Services 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Financial Aid Coordinator, Student and Office Support Apply now Job no: 503982 Work type: Nonexempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Administrative Services Financial Aid Coordinator - Join Lehigh University's Admissions Team Lehigh University's Office of Financial Aid is looking for a detail-oriented and student-focused Financial Aid Coordinator to join a collaborative enrollment support team in Bethlehem, PA. If you find genuine satisfaction in helping students and families navigate one of the most important financial decisions of their lives, this role offers meaningful daily impact within a respected research university community. About the Opportunity You'll provide administrative and clerical support to the Office of Financial Aid and Assistant Vice Provost of Financial Services and Director of Financial Aid. As an Enrollment Support Coordinator team member, you'll deliver superior customer service to students and families navigating admissions and financial aid processes. Position Number: S79290 This position is a Grade: 7 - 37.5 with an approximate salary range of $37,190-$44,640 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Responsibilities Serves as the primary liaison for the Financial Aid Office, providing professional, multi-channel support to students and families by interpreting complex federal and institutional policies alongside admissions and billing processes. Partners effectively with internal and external stakeholders to resolve inquiries, escalating issues when necessary and ensuring all interactions promote an equitable, inclusive, and service-oriented environment. Manages office logistics and supply procurement while maintaining the Financial Aid Coordinator manual and recommending process improvements to ensure an equitable, efficient, and well-documented workflow. Provides comprehensive administrative assistance to leadership and counseling staff, including complex calendar management, meeting coordination, and the preparation of petitions for the Undergraduate Financial Aid committee. Manages departmental fiscal operations by reconciling budgets, tracking OneCard transactions, processing vendor payments, and preparing documentation for financial audits to ensure compliance and budgetary integrity. Coordinates office personnel processes such as new hire documentation and payroll forms, while overseeing all logistical elements for Financial Aid events, including venue booking, catering, and materials. Guides students through summer and winter study abroad costs and financing options via individual consultations and the creation of specialized budgeting tools, guides, and worksheets. Manages the technical administration of travel grants and budgets in Banner, coordinates cash advances for transportation, and serves as the primary liaison between the Financial Aid, Bursar, and Study Abroad offices to streamline student funding. Manages the full lifecycle of work-study staff by recruiting, hiring, and onboarding students in alignment with federal and institutional regulations, including the development of job descriptions and comprehensive training manuals. Provides daily oversight and performance coaching to ensure operational accuracy and high customer service standards, while maintaining strict confidentiality in the processing of student payroll and records. Qualifications High School Diploma or GED One to three years of related work experience Customer service experience required Financial Aid experience highly preferred Previous experience working on a team preferred Ability to multitask and work in high demand/high stress environment necessary Why Choose Lehigh University Our scenic Bethlehem campus provides an inspiring workplace environment. The Lehigh Valley combines small-town charm with access to major cities like New York and Philadelphia, offering affordable living costs and rich cultural opportunities. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Lehigh University offers a comprehensive and family friendly benefits package which includes but is not limited to Health Care, Retirement and Educational benefits. Information can be found on our website. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: July 30, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Financial Aid Coordinator, Student and Office Support Bethlehem The purpose of this non-exempt position is to provide administrative and clerical support to the Office of Financial Aid and Assistant Vice Provost of Financial Services and Director of Financial Aid by performing coordinator duties. Additionally, as a member of the Enrollment Support Coordinator team, this position is expected to provide superior customer service to students and families in the areas of both Admissions and Financial Aid. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Financial Aid Coordinator, Student and Office Support Bethlehem The purpose of this non-exempt position is to provide administrative and clerical support to the Office of Financial Aid and Assistant Vice Provost of Financial Services and Director of Financial Aid by performing coordinator duties. Additionally, as a member of the Enrollment Support Coordinator team, this position is expected to provide superior customer service to students and families in the areas of both Admissions and Financial Aid. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment 