      "title": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Assistant Coach, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field",
      "description": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Assistant Coach, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Human Resources Finance & Administration Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Essentials (current) Show menu Disability Accommodations For Faculty and Staff Disability Accommodations Procedure Employee Relations When to Contact HR Reporting Bias and Harassment Employee Relations Resources Alternative Work Arrangements Flexplace and Remote Resources Lehigh Staff Flexplace Policy Staff, Researchers and Adjunct Faculty Fully Remote Policy States Approved for Fully Remote Work Employee Assistance Program Finance & Administration Inclusive Excellence and Belonging PageUp Learning, Performance and Talent User Guides Payroll Protection of Minors Compliance Report A Concern The Perch The Spot Well-Being Benefits & Rewards (current) Show menu Benefits Changes Effective January 1, 2027 Benefits Changes Taking Effect July 1, 2026 FY27 Changes to Vacation Accrual, Carryover and Payout Benefits Eligibility Staff Faculty Centennial School Employees Research Personnel Benefits-Eligible Retirees Temporary and/or Wage Employees Dependents Health Care Benefits Medical Insurance Prescription Drug Coverage Behavioral (Mental) Health Benefits Vision Care Dental Coverage Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Adult Vaccine Benefits for Lehigh Medical Plan Participants Medicare Eligibility & Your Coverage Options Worker’s Compensation Compensation Market Referenced Job Evaluation Process Lehigh Staff Salary Structure Lehigh University Compensation Philosophy Variable Pay Time Away From Work Short Term Disability Staff Paid Parental Leave Benefit Retirement And Financial Security Lehigh Retirement Plan Social Security and Medicare Basic And Supplemental Life Insurance Dependent Life Insurance Long Term Disability Insurance Educational Benefits Education Benefits For Faculty and Staff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Athletics 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Assistant Coach, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field Apply now Job no: 503983 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Athletics Lehigh University's NCAA Division I Athletics program is looking for a skilled and committed Assistant Coach to join the Men's & Women's Cross Country and Track & Field staff. If you bring a sharp coaching eye, a genuine investment in student-athlete growth, and the drive to compete at the highest level of collegiate sport, this is a role worth your attention. This position has a unique dual responsibility of serving as the primary assistant coach for the cross country, middle and distance programs while also assisting with the operational planning and execution of signature events such as the Paul Short Run, NCAA Regional Championships, and other cross country and track & field competitions hosted by Lehigh University. The position requires exceptional organizational, logistical, and event management skills in addition to high-level coaching and recruiting expertise. Position Number: S82970 This position is a Grade: 6 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $28,670-$34,410 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities Drive student-athlete success by mentoring individuals in academic, athletic, and personal growth, while fostering an inclusive team culture focused on integrity, mental wellness, leadership, and retention. Design and execute individualized, long-term training plans, deliver technical instruction and race strategy, and conduct daily practice sessions to maximize performance across cross country, indoor, and outdoor track & field seasons. Analyze athlete data to track progress, coordinate with high-performance support staff (strength, nutrition, sports medicine, and psychology), and manage on-site coaching during team travel and competitions. Identify, evaluate, and recruit high-caliber student-athletes through competitions, campus visits, video analysis, and recruiting databases to meet the specific event needs of the cross country and track & field programs. Build strong, trust-based relationships with prospective student-athletes, families, and coaches while passionately promoting Lehigh University’s academic excellence, athletic tradition, and overall student-athlete experience. Execute strategic recruiting plans focused on diversity, enrollment, and retention, while managing all recruiting workflows, correspondence, campus visit logistics, and compliance with admissions and financial aid staff. Assist with budgeting, scheduling, equipment management, and team travel logistics for the cross country and distance programs, ensuring full compliance with NCAA, Patriot League, and University policies. Co-lead the planning, logistics, and execution of the premier Paul Short Run and other hosted home meets, collaborating with external vendors and campus partners to oversee timing, facility setup, staffing, and race operations. Work alongside athletic administration, sports medicine, marketing, and campus public safety to support overall program goals, complete seasonal administrative duties (August 1–May 30), and participate in institutional initiatives. Serve as a positive brand ambassador by collaborating with Athletics Advancement and Communications to drive alumni engagement, fundraising, camps, community outreach, and the promotion of the Paul Short Run and team accomplishments. Drive sustained athletic and academic success across Patriot League and NCAA competitions while fostering student-athlete character, personal growth, retention, and graduation. Successfully execute program operations and lead the planning and management of home meets, including premier national events like the Paul Short Run and NCAA Regional Championships, in full compliance with NCAA and conference regulations. Identify and recruit elite prospective student-athletes while actively cultivating strong relationships with alumni, donors, parents, and community members to enhance the national reputation of Lehigh Athletics. Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in a related field; Master's Degree preferred One to three years of work related experience Experience as a student athlete Collegiate coaching and/or competitive experience in cross country or track & field with an emphasis on middle and distance events Demonstrated knowledge of NCAA recruiting and compliance regulations Strong organizational, communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills Commitment to supporting academic achievement and holistic student-athlete development Ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting critical deadlines Ability to fulfill the responsibilities of a full-time 10-month appointment operating from August 1 through May 30, with flexibility to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and extensive travel during the competitive season Valid driver's license and ability to satisfy University driver requirements Previous NCAA Division I coaching experience preferred Proven experience in collegiate distance coaching, large-scale cross country event management, and athletic program fundraising/alumni engagement Why Lehigh Lehigh University sits at the intersection of rigorous academic tradition and genuine athletic ambition. As part of the Athletics staff, you'll work within a department that takes the student-athlete experience seriously. Your work here shapes not just athletic results, but the character and trajectory of the individuals you coach. Lehigh University offers a comprehensive and family friendly benefits package which includes but is not limited to Health Care, Retirement and Educational benefits. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations This position is responsible for driving as a routine function, therefore a valid Driver’s License and a good driving record is required. This position has direct contact with minors, therefore a background check is required. This position has off the months of June and July Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: July 30, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Assistant Coach, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field Bethlehem The Assistant Coach for Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field provides leadership, instruction, and operational support for Lehigh University's NCAA Division I Men's and Women's Cross Country and Track & Field programs. Reporting to the Head Cross Country and Track & Field Coaches, the Assistant Coach plays a vital role in advancing the mission of Lehigh University and the Department of Athletics through excellence in coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, championship event management, and program administration. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Assistant Coach, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field Bethlehem The Assistant Coach for Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field provides leadership, instruction, and operational support for Lehigh University's NCAA Division I Men's and Women's Cross Country and Track & Field programs. Reporting to the Head Cross Country and Track & Field Coaches, the Assistant Coach plays a vital role in advancing the mission of Lehigh University and the Department of Athletics through excellence in coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, championship event management, and program administration. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. 