inance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Development/ Alumni Relations 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Director, Corporate and Foundations Relations Apply now Job no: 503963 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Development/ Alumni Relations Lehigh University's Development and Alumni Relations division is building something meaningful, a stronger bridge between one of the nation's leading research universities and the corporate and philanthropic communities that share its ambitions. If you're an experienced fundraising professional who knows how to turn institutional relationships into lasting partnerships, this is a role worth your attention. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of College Development and University Initiatives, you will take ownership of a strategic portfolio of corporate and foundation prospects, working side-by-side with academic leaders across Lehigh's colleges to align philanthropic priorities with external funding opportunities. Your work will span the full relationship cycle, from research and qualification through cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. Position Number: S84950 This position is a Grade: 11 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $83,910-$102,080 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities Identify potential corporate and foundation partners to build targeted, long-term strategies that align with college priorities. Cultivate strong relationships across all funder levels—including program officers, trustees, and C-suite executives—through regular visits and strategic outreach. Lead strategy sessions and partner with academic leaders, Development and Alumni Relations (DAR), and campus stakeholders to drive sponsored research and philanthropic support. Articulate the college’s value proposition to secure funding and provide comprehensive stewardship, including detailed reporting and host visits for institutional partners. Partner with academic leaders, faculty, alumni, and Trustees to identify, build, and leverage relationships with corporations and foundations for gifts, grants, research, and data agreements. Coordinate and facilitate high-level campus visits, executive briefings, and follow-up strategies to secure and advance strategic institutional partnerships. Partner with faculty and deans to design and package university priority initiatives for funding opportunities. Participate in university-wide training and identify growth and leadership opportunities for the Corporate and Foundation Relations (CFR) team. Write complex, budgeted proposals in partnership with stakeholders, consulting with departments to present and secure funding for priority projects. Work closely with DAR teams to streamline workflows, integrate prospect strategies, and maintain accurate records in the primary database. Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Communications, Liberal Arts, STEM or Business field Five to eights years in development, fundraising, or a related field, ideally in higher education or non-profit setting Experience with major gift fundraising, writing foundation grants and capital campaigns Ability to thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, managing multiple priorities simultaneously Excellent written and oral communications skills, with the ability to craft compelling messages and engage donors/foundations at every level Experience event planning and project management, with a track record of successfully executing events Ability to work effectively with a variety of internal and external stakeholders, including faculty, staff, alumni and leadership Proficiency in fundraising software (e.g. Blackbaud, Raiser’s Edge or similar CRM) and Microsoft Office Suite Why Lehigh Lehigh offers a genuinely distinctive environment for advancement professionals — a research-intensive university with the collegial culture of a smaller institution, located in the Lehigh Valley with accessible connections to New York and Philadelphia. Lehigh University offers a comprehensive and family friendly benefits package which includes but is not limited to Health Care, Retirement and Educational benefits. The university's continued investment in its development infrastructure means you'll have real resources behind your work. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations This position includes driving as a routine function, therefore a valid Driver’s License and a good driving record is required. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: July 30, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Director, Corporate and Foundations Relations Bethlehem Reporting to the Assistant Vice President, College Development & University Initiatives, the Director, Corporate and Foundation Relations will work closely with assigned academic leaders to identify and pursue relationships and funding opportunities. The Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations will analyze and target a strategic portfolio of foundation partners, private foundations and other organizations, manage and grow a pipeline of prospects, and drive collaboration that results in increased philanthropy, sponsored research and internship/job opportunities. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Director, Corporate and Foundations Relations Bethlehem Reporting to the Assistant Vice President, College Development & University Initiatives, the Director, Corporate and Foundation Relations will work closely with assigned academic leaders to identify and pursue relationships and funding opportunities. The Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations will analyze and target a strategic portfolio of foundation partners, private foundations and other organizations, manage and grow a pipeline of prospects, and drive collaboration that results in increased philanthropy, sponsored research and internship/job opportunities. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
    },
