      "title": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Program Director, Business Assistance Service Centers",
      "description": "Careers at Lehigh - Details - Program Director, Business Assistance Service Centers Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Human Resources Finance & Administration Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Essentials (current) Show menu Disability Accommodations For Faculty and Staff Disability Accommodations Procedure Employee Relations When to Contact HR Reporting Bias and Harassment Employee Relations Resources Alternative Work Arrangements Flexplace and Remote Resources Lehigh Staff Flexplace Policy Staff, Researchers and Adjunct Faculty Fully Remote Policy States Approved for Fully Remote Work Employee Assistance Program Finance & Administration Inclusive Excellence and Belonging PageUp Learning, Performance and Talent User Guides Payroll Protection of Minors Compliance Report A Concern The Perch The Spot Well-Being Benefits & Rewards (current) Show menu Benefits Changes Effective January 1, 2027 Benefits Changes Taking Effect July 1, 2026 FY27 Changes to Vacation Accrual, Carryover and Payout Benefits Eligibility Staff Faculty Centennial School Employees Research Personnel Benefits-Eligible Retirees Temporary and/or Wage Employees Dependents Health Care Benefits Medical Insurance Prescription Drug Coverage Behavioral (Mental) Health Benefits Vision Care Dental Coverage Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Adult Vaccine Benefits for Lehigh Medical Plan Participants Medicare Eligibility & Your Coverage Options Worker’s Compensation Compensation Market Referenced Job Evaluation Process Lehigh Staff Salary Structure Lehigh University Compensation Philosophy Variable Pay Time Away From Work Short Term Disability Staff Paid Parental Leave Benefit Retirement And Financial Security Lehigh Retirement Plan Social Security and Medicare Basic And Supplemental Life Insurance Dependent Life Insurance Long Term Disability Insurance Educational Benefits Education Benefits For Faculty and Staff Tuition Benefits For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Higher Education Administration 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Program Director, Business Assistance Service Centers Apply now Job no: 503980 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Higher Education Administration Lehigh University's Small Business Development Center (SBDC) is a cornerstone of economic vitality in the Lehigh Valley, connecting entrepreneurs with the tools and expertise they need to build lasting businesses. As Program Director for the Business Assistance Service Centers (BASC), you will shape that impact directly — leading operations across Lehigh and Northampton Counties and ensuring that every client interaction reflects the SBDC's commitment to meaningful, measurable outcomes. Reporting through the College of Business, this full-time exempt role carries broad operational and programmatic responsibility across both BASC locations. Position Number: S98340 This position is a Grade: 9 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $56,030-$68,190 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities Directing all day-to-day operations of the BASC network across Lehigh and Northampton Counties Ensuring service delivery meets program objectives and quality standards established by the Pennsylvania Department of Community and Economic Development (DCED) Managing contractual compliance, reporting cycles, and performance metrics required by state funding agreements Supervising, mentoring, and evaluating BASC staff to maintain consistent, high-quality business assistance Developing and monitoring program budgets in alignment with contractual obligations Building partnerships with regional economic development stakeholders, municipalities, and business support organizations Tracking client outcomes and preparing detailed performance reports for DCED and University leadership Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Business Administration, Economics, Entrepreneurship or related fields; Master's Degree preferred Five to eights years of work related experience Demonstrated experience directing a program, business development initiative, or economic development service Solid understanding of small business operations, entrepreneurship ecosystems, or commercial lending environments Experience managing government contracts or grant-funded programs, including compliance and performance reporting Strong relationship management skills with public sector, nonprofit, and private sector partners Proven ability to lead a team toward clearly defined service and outcome targets Fluent in Spanish (or another second language) preferred Why Lehigh Lehigh University offers a genuinely collegial environment where professional staff are valued contributors to the University's broader civic and academic mission. You'll have access to generous benefits including comprehensive health coverage, substantial retirement contributions, and tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents. The SBDC's deep integration with the College of Business means you'll work alongside faculty researchers and practitioner networks that few regional development roles can match — giving your work both community grounding and intellectual depth. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations This position is funded by soft dollars; there is no severance associated with this position. This term position, tentatively ending September 2027. Eligible for possible extension based on available funding. The duties of the position do not allow for a remote work option; the employee in this position will be required to work on campus where they can be fully accessible to the Lehigh community. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: July 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Program Director, Business Assistance Service Centers Bethlehem This position directs all operations and activities of the Lehigh SBDC’s Business Assistance Service Centers (BASC) in Lehigh and Northampton Counties.  The Program Director ensures that BASC services meet program objectives, deliver high-quality business assistance to area entrepreneurs, and comply with all contractual and reporting requirements established by the Pennsylvania Department of Community and Economic Development (DCED). Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Program Director, Business Assistance Service Centers Bethlehem This position directs all operations and activities of the Lehigh SBDC’s Business Assistance Service Centers (BASC) in Lehigh and Northampton Counties.  The Program Director ensures that BASC services meet program objectives, deliver high-quality business assistance to area entrepreneurs, and comply with all contractual and reporting requirements established by the Pennsylvania Department of Community and Economic Development (DCED). Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
