ts For Spouses/Partners Tuition Benefits For Dependent Children Tuition Benefits for Retirees Ancillary Benefits And Services Extended Health Care Benefits Lehigh Amenities and Opportunities Voluntary Benefits Work-Related Insurance Coverages Qualifying Life Events Documentation and Event Dates for QLEs Frequently Asked Benefits Questions Open Enrollment for 2026 Flexible Benefits Voluntary Benefits by Voya Learn & Grow (current) Show menu Career Enrichment Upcoming Learning Opportunities Learning Partners Nomination and High Potential Programs Professional Development Certificate Tracks LinkedIn Learning for Faculty and Staff BEST Program Performance Performance Review Process Understanding Expectations Using The Page Up Learning, Performance and Talent Portal Training for Hiring Managers Recruitment User Guides Onboarding User Guides Learning User Guides Performance User Guides Position Description User Guides Search/Apply for Positions Careers (current) Show menu New to Lehigh? Welcome! Your First Month Your First Three Months Your First Six Months Your First Year and Beyond Lehigh Lingo for Faculty/Staff Engage @Lehigh Staff and Faculty Openings Meet Our Employees Life in the Lehigh Valley Benefits Overviews for Applicants Cash for Colleagues Employee Referral Program I-9 Completion Information Food Service, Housekeeping, and Landscaping Employment Opportunities Temporary Employment FAQ: The Hiring Process at Lehigh Well-Being (current) Show menu Health Scan Smoking Cessation Resources for Benefits Eligible Employees Wellness Resources HR Jira Portal (current) Engage Lehigh (current) Show menu Recognize Awards For Exceptional Performance And Contributions Staff Service Milestones Celebrate 2026 Staff Appreciation Dinner Program Learn - Career Enrichment HR Forms (current) More Show more menu items Quick Links Quick Links About Human Resources Be Well Disability Accommodation for Staff & Faculty HR and F&A Policy Database HR Forms HR Publications Finance & Administration Links to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Higher Education Administration 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Business Assistance Specialist Apply now Job no: 503979 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Higher Education Administration Lehigh University's Small Business Development Center (SBDC) and Business Assistance Service Center (BASC) sit at the intersection of rigorous academic thinking and real-world economic impact. As a Business Assistance Specialist, you'll translate that expertise into meaningful outcomes for entrepreneurs and business owners across the region. Reporting to the Director, you'll carry a portfolio of client engagements while contributing to the Center's measurable performance targets. Position Number(s): S98470 & S99580 This position is a Grade: 9 - 40 with an approximate salary range of $56,030-$68,190 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities Delivering one-on-one consulting to startups and established businesses on strategy, business planning, and cash flow projections Conducting applied research and presenting findings directly to clients on market conditions, financing options, and industry trends Developing, coordinating, and facilitating training programs aligned to specific SBDC/BASC service offerings and client needs Monitoring and supporting progress against performance goals set by the Director across individual service areas Preparing clear written materials, reports, and presentations for clients covering a range of business topics Contributing to broader Center programs and initiatives beyond core consulting, including outreach and partnership activities Supporting documented client outcomes that meet state and federal performance benchmarks Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Business; Master's Degree preferred Five to eights years of work related experience Experience in small business consulting Practical knowledge of business plan development, financial modelling, and cash flow analysis Ability to design and deliver training content for diverse business audiences Strong research skills with the capacity to synthesize information into clear, actionable recommendations Familiarity with SBDC reporting requirements or federally funded program compliance is an advantage Willingness and ability to work evenings and/or weekends as needed during peak business periods Fluency in Spanish (or another second language) preferred Why Lehigh Lehigh University brings together a community where scholarship and civic engagement reinforce each other. As part of the College of Business, this role benefits from access to faculty research, a robust professional network, and a culture that values intellectual rigor in service of practical outcomes. Staff enjoy generous benefits including substantial retirement contributions above standard market rates, comprehensive health coverage, tuition remission opportunities, and a campus environment that takes professional development seriously. You'll work within a team that measures its success by the growth of the businesses and communities it serves. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations The duties of the position do not allow for a remote work option; the employee in this position will be required to work on campus where they can be fully accessible to the Lehigh community. This position is funded by soft dollars; there is no severance associated with this position. This is a term-limited position through September 2027 (unless otherwise extended). Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: July 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Business Assistance Specialist Bethlehem Responsible for ensuring SBDC/BASC meets specific performance goals relative to individual service offerings as determined by Director. Provides consulting services to startup and existing businesses on strategies, business plans, cash flow projections, and other related matters as well as other Center programs. Investigates prepares and presents research to client on relevant topics. Responsible for preparing and coordinating program-specific training topics. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Business Assistance Specialist Bethlehem Responsible for ensuring SBDC/BASC meets specific performance goals relative to individual service offerings as determined by Director. Provides consulting services to startup and existing businesses on strategies, business plans, cash flow projections, and other related matters as well as other Center programs. Investigates prepares and presents research to client on relevant topics. Responsible for preparing and coordinating program-specific training topics. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St