to Resources Staff/Faculty Job Openings Careers at Lehigh Breadcrumb Home Careers At Lehigh Existing Applicant Login Subscribe to Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine your search Work Type Exempt Staff Full-time 1 Locations Bethlehem 1 Categories Health Care 1 Faculty Opportunities Research Opportunities Federal Work Study Opportunities Staff Physician Apply now Job no: 503934 Work type: Exempt Staff Full-time Location: Bethlehem Categories: Health Care Lehigh University's Student Affairs division is looking for a Staff Physician who understands that a student's ability to thrive academically and personally begins with their health. Based at Lehigh's on-campus Health and Wellness Center in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, you'll deliver comprehensive primary care to a diverse community of undergraduate and graduate students — bringing clinical rigor and genuine human connection to every encounter. Working within an ambulatory health setting, you'll be the clinical anchor for students navigating everything from acute illness to ongoing chronic conditions. Position Number: S80380 This position is a Grade: 13 - 40with an approximate salary range of $136,340-$180,000 and is subject to change based on experience, skills and qualifications. Key Accountabilities Deliver evidence-based primary care by diagnosing, treating, and managing both acute and chronic conditions, including performing office-based procedures and coordinating specialty referrals. Evaluate patient health by obtaining medical histories, performing physical exams, and ordering/interpreting diagnostic tests to develop and manage tailored treatment plans and prescribe medications. Provide preventive health services—such as screenings, risk assessments, and immunizations—alongside patient-centered counseling to promote overall wellness and disease prevention. Exercise independent clinical judgment within your scope of practice to coordinate patient care, monitor progress, and dynamically adjust treatment plans to ensure high quality and continuity. Respond empathetically to complex or sensitive health concerns—such as mental and sexual health—by providing ongoing care, managing specialty referrals, and ensuring appropriate follow-up. Serve as a supervising or collaborating physician for Advanced Practice Clinicians (APCs) in accordance with state requirements while reviewing and documenting external health forms and medical data. Support efficient clinic flow within a team-based care model and actively participate in developing and implementing clinical protocols, guidelines, and service delivery enhancements. Contribute to university-wide health initiatives, outreach, and educational programming, while serving on university or Student Affairs committees dedicated to student health and wellbeing. Maintain all required professional licenses, certifications, and prescriptive authority while strictly adhering to clinical, legal, and regulatory standards such as HIPAA and infection control. Ensure high-quality patient data management by completing accurate and timely documentation within electronic medical records. Commit to continuous practice improvement by participating in quality assurance activities and maintaining clinical competency through continuing medical education and evidence-based practice. Qualifications Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) degree Three to five years of work related experience Active, unrestricted Pennsylvania state medical license Active Federal DEA registration/licensure Current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification Solid understanding of healthcare compliance requirements and clinical documentation standards A communication style that builds trust with young adults who may be managing health decisions independently for the first time Experience in college health, adolescent medicine, or a comparable setting that reflects the population and pace of Lehigh's Health and Wellness Center Why Lehigh Lehigh University has a long-standing commitment to treating its staff as integral to the institution's mission, not peripheral to it. As part of Student Affairs, you'll work alongside counselors, health educators, and wellness professionals who share your investment in student outcomes. Lehigh offers retirement contributions, comprehensive health coverage, and tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents. The residential campus in Bethlehem places you within a close, engaged community while keeping Philadelphia and New York City well within reach. Here, strong clinical practice and meaningful relationships with the people you care for go hand in hand. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate. We are committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and we seek qualified candidates to contribute to the university’s mission. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing an accommodation for any part of the interview or hiring process may contact Lehigh's Accommodations Specialist . Special Considerations This position has direct contact with minors, therefore a background check is required. Must be up-to-date on all recommended vaccination per CDC/ACIP guidelines including annual seasonal Flu vaccine unless medically exempt. Successful completion of standard background checks including but not limited to: social security verification, education verification, national criminal background checks, motor vehicle checks, PATCH, FBI fingerprinting, Child Abuse Clearance and credit history based upon the requirements of the position. Only complete applications will be considered therefore please complete the application in its entirety.  Once the posting is removed from the website applications may no longer be allowed to be completed. Advertised: July 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Staff Physician Bethlehem The Staff Physician provides comprehensive primary care to university students in an ambulatory health setting. This role is responsible for the assessment, diagnosis, and management of acute and chronic health conditions, as well as preventive care and health promotion. The Staff Physician exercises advanced clinical judgment and evidence-based practice to support student health and ensure high-quality, compliant care delivery. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Staff Physician Bethlehem The Staff Physician provides comprehensive primary care to university students in an ambulatory health setting. This role is responsible for the assessment, diagnosis, and management of acute and chronic health conditions, as well as preventive care and health promotion. The Staff Physician exercises advanced clinical judgment and evidence-based practice to support student health and ensure high-quality, compliant care delivery. Future Opportunities Don’t see a current opening which matches your interests? Feel free to create a profile and select the types of jobs that interest you. Loading... Powered by PageUp Why Lehigh? A comprehensive benefit package for you and those that you care about. Hear from Lehigh staff members what makes working here so special. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse community and interested in candidates who seek to contribute tothe university’s mission. Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Poster Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Poster Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) Poster LCA Notices of Intent to Hire H-1B/E-3 Employees In compliance with US Department of Labor requirements and pursuant to 20 CFR 655.734, Lehigh University provides notices of intent to hire non-immigrant workers in the H-1B and E-3 visa classifications. Please note candidates have already been selected to fill the positions; the Notice of Intent to Hire is not a posting for an open position. CONTACT US inemploy@lehigh.edu 610-758-3900 ASK HR Human Resources Like us on Facebook Like us on Instagram Like us on Youtube Like us on Linkedin Phone Number 610-758-3900 Fax Number 610-758-6226 Address 306 S New St, Suite 437, Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States Email address inhro@lehigh.edu User account menu Log in"
